# Maple Market

A visual, interactive, plain-English stock research tool for young novice Canadian investors (new grads / early 20s), starting with the TSX. It turns confusing market data into something you can see, play with, and understand. Visual quality, smooth interaction, and clean code matter. This is a portfolio piece as well as a learning tool.

**Core loop:** Discover → Understand → Compare → Build → Project.

**Guiding test:** Would a 22-year-old with no finance background understand this and want to keep playing with it? If a feature is just a data table, add a visual and a plain-English layer.

## What this app is NOT

- Not a trading platform. Nothing is bought or sold.
- Not a price predictor. AI explains the narrative and never promises direction.
- Not for experts. Prefer plain words over jargon, and define jargon when a number needs it.

Keep a persistent, tasteful "Educational only, not financial advice" notice in the footer and on every AI feature.

## Architecture

```
src/
  app/                  # routes + route handlers (thin)
  features/             # galaxy, scorecard, sentiment, portfolio, timemachine,
                        # retirement, dividends, compare, heatmap, quiz
  lib/
    data/               # MarketDataProvider + adapters + cache + seed
    llm/                # LLMProvider + adapters + prompts + schemas
    scoring/            # pure functions: metrics -> grades + plain English
    finance/            # pure functions: compound growth, Monte Carlo, DRIP
    storage/            # PersistenceAdapter (localStorage impl)
  components/ui/
  types/
```

- Provider pattern: `MarketDataProvider`, `LLMProvider`, `PersistenceAdapter`, and `Cache` are interfaces. Env vars choose the implementation. Feature code must not import a vendor SDK.
- All math and scoring is pure and unit-tested without network access.
- No secrets on the client. API keys live in route handlers only. Read them from `.env.local` (Next also loads `.env`). Document every variable in `.env.example`.
- TSX tickers use the `.TO` convention in the UI. Map to each provider's symbol format inside the adapter.
- Live data falls back cache, then seed. The app must work offline from seed data. Synthetic snapshots stay flagged `isSynthetic: true` and show a visible Demo data badge.
- Validate external API responses and all LLM JSON with Zod.
- Package manager is pnpm.

## Data rules

- Quotes cache about 15 minutes, history about 6 hours, fundamentals about 24 hours.
- Track per-provider rate limits. Never burn a daily quota to paint a page.
- Yahoo Finance (`yahoo-finance2`) is unofficial and for development only.
- Do not invent fake news headlines. If headlines are unavailable, say so.
